// Bug 123 review: Elab replaced a constant initializer that failed to elaborate with a silent 0
// (on main too). A borrow block on a constant inside an initializer made Y read 0; the
// elaboration error is now reported. Exit 2i: that borrow block is refused earlier, at Check
// (REF-6@1, E0302: a constant initializer may not bind a reference), so this fixture reaches
// Elab's error path with an undeclared name instead (E0401). Since exit 2i review round 15 constant
// initializers are type-checked, so Check reports the undeclared name first (E0201); the point —
// an initializer that fails is reported, never replaced by a silent 0 — holds either way.
const X: Int = 42;
const Y: Int = if true {
    let n: Int = nosuch;
    42
} else { 42 };

fn main() -> Int {
    return Y;
}
